---
const irregular = [
  ["go", "went", "come", "came"],
  ["see", "saw", "say", "said"],
  ["eat", "ate", "give", "gave"],
  ["run", "ran", "take", "took"],
  ["write", "wrote", "think", "thought"],
  ["have", "had", "do", "did"]
];
---

<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Verb Tenses - Simple past and future</h1>
  <section class="summary-block summary-blue">
    <h2>Simple past</h2>
    <p>The simple past describes an event or state that happened earlier. Many verbs add <strong>-ed</strong> (<em>play → played; jump → jumped</em>). Some spellings change (<em>live → lived; try → tried; stop → stopped</em>). Other verbs are irregular.</p>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Present</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Past</th>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Present</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Past</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          irregular.map(([a, b, c, d]) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{a}</td>
              <td>{b}</td>
              <td>{c}</td>
              <td>{d}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>He <strong>played</strong> football yesterday. They <strong>went</strong> to Dubai last year.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="summary-block summary-green">
    <h2>Simple future</h2>
    <p>Use <strong>will</strong> plus the base verb for an event expected in the future.</p>
    <p>I <strong>will visit</strong> my friend. They <strong>will study</strong> later.</p>
  </section>
</div>
